>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `term_size_bounded`

``` hol4
Term.term_size_bounded : int -> term -> int option
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Counts raw term syntax up to a caller-supplied limit.

`Term.term_size_bounded limit t` returns `SOME n` exactly when
`Term.term_size t = n` and `n <= limit`. It returns `NONE` when `limit` is
negative or the size exceeds it. Applications count once plus both children;
abstractions count once plus the body, without separately counting the binder.

The traversal is iterative and stops before incrementing beyond the limit.
In the standard kernel it exposes a delayed closure one outer constructor at a
time and does not normalize a complete abstraction body through `dest_abs`.
Its work is proportional to the raw nodes visited before the bound, plus
one-step closure-environment work and the pending traversal stack. It does not
memoize shared subterms and makes no intrinsic-DAG complexity claim. The
unbounded raw counter with the same node metric is `Term.term_size`; this is
different from the convenience counter named `HolKernel.term_size`, which
does not count application constructors.

### Failure

Never fails on a well-formed term.
